<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Palo Hincado</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1808">1808</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-reconquest-of-santo-domingo">Spanish reconquest of Santo Domingo</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Palo Hincado was fought on 7 November 1808 near El Seibo in the east of the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a>. Dominican <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">creole</a> forces led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-sanchez-ramirez">Juan Sánchez Ramírez</a>, with support from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, defeated the French troops of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-louis-ferrand">Jean-Louis Ferrand</a>, who killed himself after the battle. The victory led to the siege of Santo Domingo, which ended French rule in 1809 and returned the colony to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-palo-hincado.jpg" alt="Battle of Palo Hincado" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M@verick · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palo_Hincado_monument.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
